From 9b2fb1e9dc9e59a8a14858bce2f141393ea1baa0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:51:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sidebar): awake replica rows outside the projects tree
 get their owner's activity stamps [daveey]

With the hub active, this Mac's older chats come in as hub-replica rows with no
kanban/goal/outcome/cwd stamps. db7e385651 swapped in the projects-tree copy,
but the tree carries a few previews per project, so a parked chat outside it
(20261026_170127_f07c32) still painted no waiting stripe.

New GET /api/profiles/sessions/stamps?profile=&ids= returns the annotated
stamps (same annotators as the list endpoints) for named sessions.
owner-row-stamps.ts asks each awake owner for its replica rows' stamps
(throttled 30s/row, 120s backoff on failure, batches of 100) and
mergeOfflineFallback folds them into the replica row. Asleep (offline_cached)
rows are untouched; a tree copy still wins.
